r in between workouts  animal products and animal proteins tend  to be acid forming foods and so your pH  becomes more acidic which is which  really impedes your but your body's  ability to repair itself and recover  when I decided to do triathlon I was  thrilled to see an article written by  rich on the front page of cnn.com  I knew I had a lot to learn from this  amazing vegan endurance athlete  as a result of the CNN piece I got  unbelievable number of emails from  people who really want you know a  solution now it's just a fad diet but  you know a real lasting permanent way to  change their habits that's going to have  long-term health benefits you know  prevent heart disease turn off cancer  cells to prevent diabetes like all these  sort there's just you know a litany of  amazing you know health benefits and  reasons why it's a good idea so you know  I would like to say to everybody out  there that not only is it an option for  you I would you know I think that it's  advisable and that you know maybe you  should try it for 30 days and see what  you think one of the biggest things that  that that I'm learning more and more  about is factory farming and the the  environmental implications of eating a  plant-based diet you know the way that  our food is prepared the way it's made  and the way that animals are treated in  that and it's been you know shocking and  eye-opening you know the biggest impact  I think that you can have on the  environment is avoiding animal products  in your diet what is your favorite place  to Train right here  yeah we live in the Santa Monica  Mountains in Malibu Canyon and it's  paradise for trail running and cycling  and swimming you know state park terrain  with you know hundreds and hundreds of  miles of beautiful untouched trails for  running and it's you know it's really  meditative and beautiful so can you tell  us a little bit about 2010 what are some  of the races you're considering well I'm  gonna have to I'm not sure yet I me